      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A survey is given on epidemiological and experimental results of lack of exercise as a risk factor for coronary heart disease. The consequences of endurance training are described. It is evident that endurance sport or training during leisure time can have a greater effect than heavy muscular professional work. The selectively analysed factor \"lack of exercise\" may be less important as a risk factor than the protective influence of endurance training. Directions are given for carrying out a preventive program of training, with contraindications included."},
